=== whatever the network does to the boundaries
pieces of 1 byte(s) yield the same pages: ok
pieces of 3 byte(s) yield the same pages: ok
pieces of 7 byte(s) yield the same pages: ok
pieces of 17 byte(s) yield the same pages: ok
pieces of 64 byte(s) yield the same pages: ok
pieces of 284 byte(s) yield the same pages: ok

=== a blank line is not a page
and is dropped rather than parsed: ok

=== a stream that stops early
is not mistaken for one that finished: ok

=== a body that ends exactly on its terminator
terminates: ok
and leaves nothing buffered: ok

=== a failure the status line could not carry
the pages before it still arrive: ok
the failure arrives as a line: ok
and the stream is not terminated: ok

=== a key that would break the framing if it could
survives a key holding a newline, a tab and a quote: ok

